  "tempo": 1.12,
  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "The cabin lights go down before a night landing,",
      "start": 0.071,
      "end": 1.928
    },
    {
      "text": "and it reads as mood lighting or saving power.",
      "start": 2.233,
      "end": 4.233
    },
    {
      "text": "It is neither.",
      "start": 4.522,
      "end": 5.093
    },
    {
      "text": "Eyes take several minutes to adapt to darkness,",
      "start": 5.416,
      "end": 7.415
    },
    {
      "text": "and takeoff and landing are when an evacuation",
      "start": 7.719,
      "end": 9.772
    },
    {
      "text": "is most likely to be needed.",
      "start": 9.808,
      "end": 10.915
    },
    {
      "text": "If the cabin were brightly lit and the power",
      "start": 11.243,
      "end": 13.192
    },
    {
      "text": "went,",
      "start": 13.244,
      "end": 13.566
    },
    {
      "text": "everyone aboard would be effectively blind",
      "start": 13.717,
      "end": 15.343
    },
    {
      "text": "at the worst possible moment.",
      "start": 15.378,
      "end": 16.681
    },
    {
      "text": "Dimming early means your eyes are already adjusted,",
      "start": 17.025,
      "end": 19.152
    },
    {
      "text": "and the floor path lighting reads",
      "start": 19.527,
      "end": 20.705
    },
    {
      "text": "clearly instead of washing out.",
      "start": 20.988,
      "end": 22.488
    },
    {
      "text": "The lights go down so you can see.",
      "start": 22.75,
      "end": 24.124
    }
  ],
